<.shell title="Layout" current={:layout}>
  <h1>Layout</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every team page starts with the same header, and content stops at a readable width.
  </p>

  <h2>Page header</h2>
  <p>Breadcrumbs, then the title.</p>
  <div class="demo">
    <.breadcrumbs team={sample_team()}>
      <:item label="Activities" path="#" />
      <:item label="25-0412" />
    </.breadcrumbs>
    <h1 class="title">Missing hiker, Stawamus Chief</h1>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.breadcrumbs&gt;</code>, then an <code>h1</code>
    with <code>class="title"</code>, which keeps 16px under it. A page's actions sit with its content, not in the header.
  </p>

  <h2>A heading with an action</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="heading-row">
      <h2 class="heading">Organizations</h2>
      <.button variant={:success} size={:sm}>New organization</.button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>.heading-row</code>: the heading on the left, its action on the right, wrapping on a phone.
  </p>

  <h2>A picture beside its words</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="media">
      <img src={~p"/images/sarduty-logo.svg"} alt="" class="logo-md" />
      <div>
        <p class="subheading mb-0">Squamish SAR</p>
        <p class="hint mb-0">BC Search and Rescue Association</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>.media</code>: a logo or photo, then its words, centred. Photos and logos use
    <code>.photo</code>, <code>.photo-sm</code>, <code>.logo-md</code>, and <code>.logo-lg</code>, or a
    size from the <a href={page_path(:spacing)}>spacing</a> scale, such as <code>size-6</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Page width</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Content fills up to 960px; tables use the full width.</li>
    <li>
      Text, forms, and maps stop at 640px with <code>.measure</code>, so lines stay readable. An article uses <code>max-w-prose</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      A record's page puts its <a href={page_path(:detail_list)}>details</a> in a sidebar beside the main
      content: <code>.content-wrapper</code>, with <code>.content-1/3</code> and <code>.content-2/3</code>.
    </li>
    <li>Desktop first. On a phone, layouts stack and wide tables scroll sideways.</li>
  </ul>
</.shell>
